<title>USA: Ryder names U.S. admiral as head of logistics.</title>
<headline>Ryder names U.S. admiral as head of logistics.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ryder System Inc said on Monday it has appointed retired U.S. Vice Admiral Edward Straw as head of its Ryder Integrated Logistics Inc unit.</p>
<p>Straw, a 1961 graduate of the U.S. Naval Academy, replaces Larry Mulkey, who is retiring, the company said in a news release.</p>
<p>Straw's last government assignment through last autumn was as director of the Defense Logistics Agency, a procurement organization with 49,000 workers and an operating budget of $14 billion.</p>
<p>((-Michael Connor - 305-374-5013))</p>
